{{title}}\ndate: {{date:YYYY-MM-DD}}\ntags: [daily]\n---\n\n# {{title}}\n\n**Date:** {{date:dddd, MMMM D, YYYY}}\n**Time created:** {{time:HH:mm}}\n\n## Top Priorities\n- [ ] \n- [ ] \n- [ ] \n\n## Schedule / Notes\n- \n\n## Log\n- \n\n## Gratitude / Wins\n- \n\n## Tomorrow\n- [ ] \n```\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Save this as `Templates/Daily Note.md`.\n2. Go to **Settings → Daily notes** and set *Template file location* to `Templates/Daily Note`.\n3. Set the *Date format* to `YYYY-MM-DD` so the title and filename match the date.\n\n## Templater plugin version\n\nIf you use Templater, these dynamic tags work well:\n\n```markdown\n---\ntitle: <% tp.file.title %>\ndate: <% tp.date.now(\"YYYY-MM-DD\") %>\ntags: [daily]\n---\n\n# <% tp.file.title %>\n\n**Date:** <% tp.date.now(\"dddd, MMMM D, YYYY\") %>\n**Time created:** <% tp.date.now(\"HH:mm\") %>\n\n[[<% tp.date.yesterday(\"YYYY-MM-DD\") %>]] ← Yesterday | Tomorrow → [[<% tp.date.tomorrow(\"YYYY-MM-DD\") %>]]\n\n## Top Priorities\n- [ ] \n\n## Schedule / Notes\n- \n\n## Log\n- \n```\n\nTo have it apply automatically, enable **Trigger Templater on new file creation** in Templater's settings, and add a *Folder Template* mapping your daily notes folder to this template.\n\n## Notes\n- `{{title}}` is the note's filename without the extension.\n- `{{date:FORMAT}}` accepts any Moment.js format string.\n- If you use a different app (Notion, Logseq, Bear, etc.), tell me and I'll adapt the syntax."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":575},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f8a3cb5-39fe-43c9-a9c2-b3a8736f501d","uuid":"7919a9dd-fd08-4cae-8860-b07c62b3d369","timestamp":"2026-10-15T15:22: